# Original environmental poses — C31 and C32

Eighteen original static drawings extend the existing Selenite costume family: recoil, retreat and regroup for the small C31 swarmer and C32 spear guard, each in front, right-side and back facings. The [contact sheet](repulsion_contact_sheet.png) displays the exact native drawings at nearest 3× scale. The [manifest](repulsion_manifest.json) records every PNG's hash, dimensions, bounds, feet pivot, source provenance and readiness. The [inert authored source](authored_repulsion_source.py.txt) preserves the drawing coordinates and primitive-reuse attribution for review.

G10, G25 and F10 were personally inspected as actual images. The original 30 poses were personally inspected in their existing contact sheet, and all 30 native cells were checked against those original PNGs. New pixels use hand-authored integer geometry and the existing seven-gray palette, mask, rib, limb and headpiece drawing primitives. No reference image pixels were extracted, sampled, cropped, edited or traced. G10 and G25 are generated planning images; F10 is a reproduction of a 1902 film frame. The monochrome palette is the game's interpretation.

| Role | Native grid | Feet pivot | Centered Sprite3D offset | Pixel size | Full native quad |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| C31 / A1-E2 swarmer | 48 × 80 px | (24, 80) px | (0, 40) px | 0.022 units/px | 1.056 × 1.76 units |
| C32 / A1-E3 spear guard | 80 × 80 px | (40, 80) px | (0, 40) px | 0.022 units/px | 1.76 × 1.76 units |

RGBA alpha is exactly 0 or 255. All opaque art stays inside the top and lateral frame edges. A planted boot reaches row 79 in every drawing; the foot origin stays at row 80. The lifted retreat boot is a cosmetic pose inside that retained frame. No body/root transform, collider, travel, velocity, turn, stat, damage or timing value is authored here. Use nearest sampling and the existing unit-scale actor presentation binding. Left-side mirroring remains a future use of the existing runtime leaf convention.

| Pose | Static visual intent |
| --- | --- |
| Recoil | Intact living actor shields its upper body; the guard tucks its carried spear beside the body. |
| Retreat | An outward-looking stride and raised hand read as leaving; the guard carries a broad spearhead below the mask. |
| Regroup | A calmer planted stance restores the costume silhouette; the guard lowers its spear. |

These are presentation labels proposed for the reviewed environmental API3 hooks. They do not replace warning → lock → active → recovery, define a timer or imply an attack. Actual native state and facing must select them. Spores remain harmless repulsion of living enemies. No field, cloud, cue, shadow, footprint, source marker, particles, hit flash or death effect is baked into these sprites.

The author inspected all 18 new contact-sheet cells: masks, ribs, complete headpieces and broad spearheads remain readable at static scale. There has been no import, runtime binding, engine execution or spore portrait test for these pixels. Before use, the owner must review the actual images, bind only after the native API3 hooks are reviewed, retain full-quad public art/camera custody, and check all new poses in the actual portrait alongside source, footprint, Hero and safe landing. Opaque pixel bounds do not replace the complete native quad for that framing check.

The original 30 PNGs, their contact sheet, generator and manifest remain unchanged. Existing evidence archives remain immutable. These new assets establish no full L3 acceptance, field placement, crowd viability, route/save behavior, equipment/profile coverage, human balance or performance result.
